{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Gerrit 3509 patch set 1: LLM-Review +1 with 3 advisory, resolved comments. Recorded here, not amended, because a new patch set would reset the votes. (1) Windows ignores the low 2 bits of a pid, so OpenProcess(1..3) would behave like pid 0. A corrupt stamp carrying pid 1-3 could then read dead instead of falling to the age ceiling; widening the guard to pid < 4 is a one-line follow-up if wanted. (2)/(3) spawn_python/stop keep no handle on the interpreter after stop(), so on Windows its pid could in principle be reused before a 'not-running' assertion. That has not been observed (Windows run 44900371740 passed both holder tests)."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1795269058259753001,"uuid":"a80608d9-1f38-4b08-86b0-fdae833411ea"}